  <data name="UIModel_DiagTrackService_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Enable telemetry related service (DiagTrack)</value>
  </data>
  <data name="UIModel_DiagTrackService_Description" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Configure "Connected User Experiences and Telemetry" (DiagTrack) service and connection for the Unified Telemetry Client Outbound Traffic. Disabling "Connected User Experiences and Telemetry" service (DiagTrack) can cause you not being able to get Xbox achievements anymore and affects Feedback Hub.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="UIModel_DiagnosticDataLevel_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Configure Windows level of diagnostic data gathering</value>
  </data>
  <data name="UIModel_DiagnosticDataLevel_Description" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>As a part of using Windows, your device sends Microsoft a limited set of data that is necessary to keep your device and operating system secure, up to date, and working as expected. In addition to creating a policy in the Windows registry, SophiApp 2.0 also displays applied policy in the Local Group Policy Editor (if the gpedit.msc snap-in is available on the system). This allows you to see which policies have been applied without having to search for keys in the Windows registry.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="UIModel_DiagnosticDataLevel_Title_1" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Default</value>
  </data>
  <data name="UIModel_DiagnosticDataLevel_Title_2" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Minimal</value>
  </data>
  <data name="UIModel_ErrorReporting_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Configure Windows Error Reporting</value>
  </data>
  <data name="UIModel_ErrorReporting_Description" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Error reporting feature enables users to notify Microsoft of application faults, kernel faults, unresponsive applications, and other application specific problems. Microsoft can use error reporting feature to provide customers with troubleshooting information, solutions, or updates for their specific problems.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="UIModel_FeedbackFrequency_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Configure feedback frequency</value>
  </data>
  <data name="UIModel_FeedbackFrequency_Title_1" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Automatically</value>
  </data>
  <data name="UIModel_FeedbackFrequency_Title_2" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Never</value>
  </data>
  <data name="UIModel_FeedbackFrequency_Description" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Choose how often Windows asks for your feedback.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="UIModel_ScheduledTasks_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Enable diagnostic tracking tasks</value>
  </data>
  <data name="UIModel_ScheduledTasks_Description" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Enable following telemetry related scheduled tasks in Task Scheduler: MareBackup, Microsoft Compatibility Appraiser, StartupAppTask, ProgramDataUpdater, Proxy, Consolidator, UsbCeip, Microsoft-Windows-DiskDiagnosticDataCollector, Microsoft-Windows-DiskDiagnosticDataCollector, MapsToastTask, MapsUpdateTask, FamilySafetyMonitor, FamilySafetyRefreshTask, XblGameSaveTask.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="UIModel_SigninInfo_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Use sign-in info to automatically finish setting up device after an update</value>
  </data>
  <data name="UIModel_SigninInfo_Description" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Some updates require you to restart your PC and afterwards sign in to Windows in order to finish installing update, which means you might not be able to use your PC until update is finished. Windows helps prevents this by allowing Windows to use your sign in info to create a special token. This token is used to automatically sign in after a restart, finish setting up your PC, and then lock your PC to keep your account and personal info safe.</value>
  </data>
